WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:12.340
39. The Dancing Plants of Yudhantani. Yes, you read that right. Plants that dance.

2
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:18.460
It's true. I've seen them. Yudhantani is a province in northeast Thailand. There are

3
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:23.340
no big cities there and not as many tourist attractions as there are in other parts of

4
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:29.540
the country. But there is one small plant nursery with one of the most amazing, but

5
00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:36.260
little known, sites in the world. Simple green plants that look like common weeds. These

6
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:42.500
particular dancing plants are a hybrid of the Tani gyrant and the Chinese gyrant. The

7
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:48.080
pure parents can't dance as well as their hybrid child. The scientific name of this

8
00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:55.900
type of plant is Codariocalyx motorius. Let's go back to the dancing. Walk through the nursery,

9
00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:01.000
which is full of beautiful Thai orchids. Deep in the center of the nursery, surrounded

10
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:07.020
by brighter, more eye-catching plants, is a row of these green weeds. These are the

11
00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:13.660
dancing plants. Stand in front of them and sing, the nursery worker says. At first it

12
00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:21.220
feels silly to sing to a plant. I sing quietly and shyly and nothing happens. I think about

13
00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:28.140
leaving, but I make myself stay and sing longer. Slowly the plants start opening and

14
00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:35.280
closing their little leaves. The longer and louder I sing, the more they move. When I

15
00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:42.540
stop, they stop. I test to see if my breath is making the leaves blow. Nope. They're moving

16
00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:48.980
because I'm making a sound. It's incredible to interact with a plant this way. It makes

17
00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:56.220
me think very deeply about the ways all living creatures are alive. Perhaps we're more connected

18
00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:03.460
with the plant world than we think we are. Why the plant dances is still mysterious,

19
00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:08.140
just another sign that we still have a lot to learn about our world.
